// Renovate, for this repository.
//
// Everything general - when updates arrive, what groups with what, what may
// merge itself - lives in Lautstark/.github and names no package. This file is
// the part that is true of this repository and of no other.
//
// The .json5 is spelled out on purpose: the //path/to/file syntax implies a
// .json extension, so omitting it looks for a file that is not there and
// Renovate stops before it does anything. The shorter "owner/repo:name" form
// implies it too.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THE SHARED PRESET COVERS HERE, AND WHAT IT SAYS IT DOES NOT
//
// The preset's own header says: "NOT COVERED: Gradle, Kotlin, Android. The
// Android repository does not exist yet, and a preset written against a guess
// about its build is a preset that will be wrong when it arrives."
//
// It has arrived, and the note turns out to have been about the wrong half.
// Nothing in the preset is npm-specific: the schedule, the dependency
// dashboard, the dev-versus-runtime split, the major-on-its-own rule and the
// vulnerability handling are all written against `matchDepTypes` and
// `matchUpdateTypes`, which the Gradle manager populates the same way. So
// extending it is right and adds no Gradle rules by omission.
//
// What is genuinely absent is a *Lautstark* opinion about Gradle, and there is
// none to write yet. When one appears - a Kotlin/AGP pairing that has to move
// together, say - it belongs here first and moves to the preset only once a
// second repository needs it.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TWO PINS RENOVATE DOES NOT SEE, NAMED SO NOBODY ASSUMES IT DOES
//
// This is the reason this file is not one line. Both are real version pins,
// both go stale silently, and neither is a dependency any manager recognises:
//
//   gradle.properties: exchange.sha
//     The conformance fixtures, pinned to a commit in
//     Lautstark/vorlaut-editor and fetched at build time. A bare SHA in a
//     properties file - no manager reads it, and no custom manager is
//     configured for it deliberately. docs/exchange-pin.md explains why:
//     moving it is a decision about which revision of the spec this viewer
//     claims to meet, and the suite failing is how that decision gets made.
//     A pull request that merged itself on a Monday morning would be the
//     wrong shape for it, the same way @lautstark/* bumps are elsewhere.
//
//   app/src/main/kotlin/de/lautstark/vorlaut/app/design/
//     The design tokens, a port of Lautstark/design rather than a dependency
//     on it. Tokens.kt names its source and the accent it was generated from,
//     which is the provenance Lautstark/design's own conventions.md §7 asks
//     for - but no version, because a generated file may not carry one. In the
//     three browser products the version lives in the pin in package.json, and
//     `pins.js` reads it and says which pins are behind. There is no pin here
//     to read. So this port going stale is the one drift in the family that
//     nothing reports, and no Renovate configuration can be the thing that
//     changes that.
//
// Neither is a rule Renovate could carry. They are here because a renovate.json5
// reads as "these are the dependencies, and they are watched", and in this
// repository two of the things most worth watching are outside it.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: ["github>Lautstark/.github//renovate-shared.json5"],
}
